<title>FRANCE: Four percent of Sidel placed - mkt sources.</title>
<headline>Four percent of Sidel placed - mkt sources.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Market sources say that 1.1 million shares in French drinks package machinery firm Sidel, amounting to four percent of the capital, were placed on Friday at a price of 400 francs each.</p>
<p>The company declined all comment when contacted.</p>
<p>&quot;A placement was carried out on 1.1 million shares in sidel at 400 francs,&quot; said one market source.</p>
<p>Sidel shares stood 2.40 percent higher at 402.9 francs at 1356 GMT.</p>
<p>On December 31, 1996, Sidel's capital broke down as follows:</p>
<p>    Management.......  10.9 percent</p>
<p>    Gaz et Eau.......  16.7 pct</p>
<p>    Cita.............   8.6 pct</p>
<p>    Banexi (BNP).....   1.2 pct</p>
<p>Various including staff.........   0.1 pct</p>
<p>    Public...........  62.5 pct</p>
</text>
